# Check out LF on every platform.
#
# framework-generator writes LF, and generated-framework/ is committed. With
# Windows' core.autocrlf=true, git would check those files out as CRLF and the
# very next generator run would rewrite all 74 of them — showing as "modified"
# with no content change at all. Pinning eol=lf keeps the working tree and the
# generator's output byte-identical, so a re-run after an unchanged map really
# does report zero writes.
* text=auto eol=lf
